{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/07 19:00 SAST
Version: 0.6
Description:
  Training Courses: the courses this company has bought access to for its staff.

  The counterpart to Company Courses, which is what the company owns and sells. The two were one
  list called "Courses" meaning owned or credited, and they are opposites - one is stock the company
  sells, the other is stock it consumes - so a single list could answer neither question. See
  ROADMAP section 3d.

  A row is an entitlement rather than a course record, which is why it carries figures a catalogue
  row does not: how many seats were bought, how many are still free, and how many staff are on the
  course or have finished it. Those are the numbers an administrator needs before deciding whether
  to approve a request or buy more.

  Core owns this markup. Themes style it through the ordinary platform table classes.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code. Each of those is read as markup rather than as text.

Changelog:
  2026/09/07 19:00 SAST
  - Created by splitting Company Courses into what the company owns and what it has bought.
#}
{% include '@platform/partials/dataset-search.html.twig' with {ds_name: 'training', ds_label: 'Search training courses', ds_value: training_search, ds_action: '/company/training'} %}

<div id="training-region" data-server-search-target>
<div id="training-results">

	{% if training_pagination %}
		{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: training_pagination} %}
	{% endif %}

	<div class="notice">
		<span>ⓘ</span>
		<div><strong>Courses this company has bought access to.</strong> Each row shows how many seats were purchased and how many are still free to assign. Courses this company owns are under <a href="/company/courses">Courses Created</a> and cost nothing to train staff on.</div>
	</div>

	{% if training %}
		<div class="table-wrap">
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr>{% for sh in training_sort_headers %}{% include '@platform/partials/sortable-header.html.twig' with {sh: sh, sort_region: training_region, sort_results: training_results} %}{% endfor %}</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{% for course in training %}
							<tr>
								<td><strong>{{ course.title }}</strong><div class="muted small">{{ course.owner_company_name ?: 'Platform course' }}</div></td>
								<td>{{ course.category_name ?: '—' }}</td>
								<td>{{ course.credits_bought }}</td>
								<td><strong>{{ course.credits_bought - course.credits_used }}</strong></td>
								<td>{{ course.staff_enrolled }}</td>
								<td>{{ course.staff_completed }}</td>
							</tr>
						{% endfor %}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>{% else %}
			<div class="empty">
				<h3>No training courses yet</h3>
				<p>When this company buys access to a course it does not own, it appears here with the seats it holds.</p>
			</div>
	{% endif %}

	{% if training_pagination %}
		{% include '@platform/partials/pagination.html.twig' with {pg: training_pagination} %}
	{% endif %}

</div>
</div>
